        <profile name="Leader" id="d2bb-aa29-abdc-e4c1" hidden="false" typeId="9cc3-6d83-4dd3-9b64" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9b8f-694b-e5e-b573">The unit gains the Leader ability.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Pack Leader" id="62f2-5fea-771e-8ee8" hidden="false" typeId="9cc3-6d83-4dd3-9b64" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9b8f-694b-e5e-b573">You can: While this model is leading a unit:
  Select one of the following:
    - You can re-roll the Charge roll.
    - You can re-roll the Advance roll.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Prey of the Blood God" id="db26-b0d5-fa29-d8e2" hidden="false" typeId="9cc3-6d83-4dd3-9b64" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9b8f-694b-e5e-b573">-&gt; At the start of the battle round, if during the first battle round:
  -&gt; Select one enemy unit, binding it as prey selection (your Prey target). When your Prey target is destroyed, you must select one enemy unit, binding it as prey selection to replace it. Only one such designation can be active for this bearer unit. For the rest of the battle, each time a model in this unit makes an attack against it, while making melee attacks, while the unit is a prey, you can re-roll the Wound roll.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Deep Strike" id="0d33-3537-06cb-6cfc" hidden="false" typeId="9cc3-6d83-4dd3-9b64" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9b8f-694b-e5e-b573">When the unit ends an ingress move, while the unit has the Deep Strike ability, the triggering unit can be set up on the battlefield more than 8" away from all enemy models.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
